From aa7b21421cf21eb50afa7fc7c3df04c97a8b61e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:14:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A plain message no longer waits 6 s for the day's optional
 contact question
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 62839 (threads 55510–55512): three plain list requests took
16.2 / 17.5 / 21.8 s. The prompt build took 6–9 s of each, and the log
says why: „[curiosity] queue gave up after 6000ms". The day's contact
question is a nice-to-have; its queue was built from scratch on every
message, and every message waited the full 6 s for it before going
without.

The queue is now built once per owner in the background and its result
kept for 10 minutes. A message waits at most 1.5 s for a build still
running; if it cannot wait, it goes without the question, and the next
message gets the finished queue.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
